# Full-resolution basemaps are ~100 MB each and regenerate in seconds from the
# terrain capture tool. The 2400px overviews the app actually loads ARE tracked,
# so cloning this repo gives you something that runs without a separate download.
*_full.png

# Raw elevation data - large, and regenerated by pressing F10 in game.
*.f32

# Editor / OS noise
.vs/
.vscode/
*.user
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Desktop shell build output. The shell is a few files of C#; the outputs are
# hundreds of megabytes once the planner's assets are copied in beside it.
shell/bin/
shell/obj/
shell/publish/

# Release archives. Built from shell/publish and uploaded to a GitHub release,
# which is where a 100 MB+ binary belongs - git rejects files over 100 MB and
# would carry every past build forever even if it did not.
shell/*.zip

# Release notes are written per release and handed to gh; the release page is
# where they live afterwards, not the working tree.
shell/notes.md

# Python bytecode from running the tools
__pycache__/
